{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786972827,"nonce":"smw7LL9dEdP5/kQT6ijILS+Q43M=","message":"Landed in `a9b412c`.\n\n`PageHeading` in `surfaces.tsx` carries a brush, background or underline, in muted or accent, from two purpose-drawn assets. The tint is a token, never a literal. §M.9 records the measured composites and `ink.test.ts` recomputes them, so the headroom argument is a gate rather than a claim: 12.95:1 and 12.21:1 in light, 10.89:1 and 10.08:1 in dark, against a 4.5:1 floor.\n\nPanel headers stay ruled. `PanelHeader`, `PanelTitle` and `SECTION_LABEL` are in the same file with the reason written between them, and §M.9 states the rule in the form the ticket asked for: **ink goes behind a page heading and nowhere else**.\n\n**Two corrections to the ticket's premise, both from the tree rather than from taste.**\n\n1. `alerts.tsx`, `groups.tsx`, `settings.tsx` and `notifications.tsx` have no page heading at all — the only `text-page` `\u003ch1\u003e`s in the product are `alert-detail.tsx:162` and `group-detail.tsx:137` (plus the proto preview). Those two are what carry a brush. The other four render panel titles, which this ticket puts out of scope anyway, so nothing was left undone; the file list was just stale.\n\n2. The two shapes needed two tint *weights*, not one. A `rule` sits beside the text rather than behind it, so it owes contrast nothing — and at the heading's 12% a 4 px tapered stroke is invisible, with the surviving fraction reading as a `border-bottom`. `--oto-wash-rule`/`-accent` are 48% for that reason and §M.9 states the axis as occupancy. This was only visible by rendering it.\n\nShape per call site, and both are argued rather than alternated: alert detail takes the **swipe** because its heading is alone on its line; group detail takes the **rule** because its heading shares a wrap row with a severity mark and three chips, and a background pass under that is one texture too many.\n\nHue: both `muted`. `accent` is implemented and legal under §M.2 and is **unspent** — recorded as such in the component and in §M.9, with ADR 0032's caveat that the two hues are kincha gold against beni crimson in light and nearly the same colour in dark. That collapse is now visible side by side in the `/proto/ui-preview` ink band.\n\nThe overshoot is `xs` in and `xl` out — 6 px and 24 px, the §M.8 spacing scale's nearest pair to the 7/22 the drawings were made at, rather than two brackets.","files":null}]}